    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners`, drawn from `owners.POST.yml` and each function class it names. Every step runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the whole thing is one transaction that commits once at the very end.\n\n## Pre-pipeline gate\n\n1. **Authorization** (`composition.authorize`) \u2014 caller must satisfy `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`; otherwise `AuthorizationDeniedException`.\n2. **Bean validation of the request body** (`@Valid OwnerFieldsDto` in `BuildOwner`) \u2014 fails with `MethodArgumentNotValidException` (400) if any constraint is violated:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, pattern `^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, pattern `^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,20)`, pattern `^[-0-9+() ]*$`\n   - `email` \u2014 optional, `@Size(max=255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 optional, pattern `^[0-9]{4}$`\n   - `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 `@Valid` (well-formed dates)\n\n## Step `build` \u2192 `BuildOwner`\n\n3. **Normalize telephone to E.164** (`E164.normalize`) \u2014 strips spaces/dashes/brackets, keeps/derives country code (defaults `+61`, drops a leading `0`), requires 8\u201315 digits and a country-code-correct national length; else `InvalidTelephoneException`. *Side effect: mutates the request's telephone.*\n4. **Normalize address** (`Address.normalize`) \u2014 trims/collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`; a value blank after collapsing throws `AddressRequiredException`. *Side effect: mutates the request's address.*\n5. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`) \u2014 *side effect: constructs the entity (id/pets ignored).*\n6. **Reject a future registration date** \u2014 if `registrationDate` is after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException`.\n7. **Default + business-day roll-forward of registration date** \u2014 null defaults to today; a Saturday/Sunday advances to the next Monday (`BusinessDay.rollForward`). *Side effect: sets `registrationDate`.*\n8. *Side effect:* publishes the built `Owner` and a `sharesHousehold` boolean for later steps.\n\n## Step `ensureEmailNotDisposable` \u2192 `EnsureOwnerEmailNotDisposable`\n\n9. **Reject disposable email domains** \u2014 domain in `{mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com}` \u2192 `DisposableEmailException`. No email is accepted.\n\n## Step `ensurePostcodeWithinRegion` \u2192 `EnsureOwnerPostcodeWithinRegion`\n\n10. **Reject postcode outside its region range** \u2014 region derived from city/locality (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099); out of range \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException`. No postcode / unknown region is accepted.\n\n## Step `ensureUniqueIdentity` \u2192 `EnsureOwnerIdentityUnique`\n\n11. **Reject a full identity-key duplicate** \u2014 loads all owners; conflict when another owner shares the whole `IdentityKey` (`telephone | email | householdId`) \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException`. A shared telephone, email, or household *alone* is allowed.\n\n## Step `ensureHouseholdUnique` \u2192 `EnsureOwnerHouseholdUnique`\n\n12. **Reject a duplicate household** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold` was set, another owner with the same `HouseholdId` (normalized last name + postcode) \u2192 `DuplicateHouseholdException`.\n\n## Step `ensureCityCapacity` \u2192 `EnsureOwnerCityWithinCapacity`\n\n13. **Reject a city at capacity** \u2014 city (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed) already holding \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n## Step `ensureDailyLimit` \u2192 `EnsureDailyOwnerLimitNotExceeded`\n\n14. **Reject once the daily limit is hit** \u2014 \u2265 100 existing owners already share the (rolled-forward) registration date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException`.\n\n## Step `assignCustomerCode` \u2192 `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`\n\n15. *Side effect:* sets `customerCode = <REGION>-<HASH8>`, where HASH8 is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`.\n\n## Step `save` \u2192 `SaveOwner`\n\n16. *Side effect:* persists the owner via `ownerRepository.save` (assigns the id).\n\n## Step `respond` \u2192 `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n\n17. *Side effects (all computed and written onto the response DTO):*\n    - `namesakeCount` \u2014 earlier owners sharing first+last name (`Namesakes.countBefore`)\n    - `membershipPoints` and `membershipLevel` (`MembershipLevel`, using namesake count and household size)\n    - `bulkSignupWarning` \u2014 > 80 owners share the registration date (`BulkSignup`)\n    - `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` \u2014 soft last-name+postcode match with a different phone (`PossibleDuplicate`)\n18. *Side effect:* writes an `AUDIT` log line (`owner created id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026 membershipLevel=\u2026`).\n19. **Responds `201 Created`** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the `OwnerDto` body.\n\nThen the transaction commits.\n\nTwo notes worth flagging: the standalone `EnsureOwnerEmailUnique` and `EnsureOwnerTelephoneUnique` classes exist in the package but are **not** wired into this pipeline \u2014 uniqueness is enforced only by the consolidated `IdentityKey` check (step 11). And the `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` mapping at step 17 additionally derives read-only fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `householdId`, `identityKey`, `membershipNumber`, `checkDigit`, `locality`, `ageBand`, `telephoneDisplay`) as part of building the response."
